---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
import { company } from '../data/site'

/**
 * Written to describe what this business and this website actually do, rather
 * than pasted from a generator. That matters: a policy describing cookies you
 * do not set and analytics you do not run is worse than none, because it is
 * demonstrably untrue of the site it sits on.
 *
 * TODO before you run paid ads or sell into the EU or UK: have somebody
 * qualified read this. If you add analytics, a chat widget, or a form, this
 * page has to change the same day.
 */
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy"
  intro="What we collect, why, and what we will never do with it. Written in plain English, because a policy nobody can read is not a policy."
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies, runs no analytics, and has no tracking pixels
    or advertising tags on it. There is no form to fill in. If you want to reach
    us you use an email link or a phone number, and nothing about your visit is
    recorded on our side until you do.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect when you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email or call, we hold what you send us: your name, your email
    address or phone number, your company, and whatever you tell us about your
    business. We use it to answer you and, if you become a customer, to run
    your service. That is the whole purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect if you become a customer</h2>
  <p>
    Running phone answering for you means handling records of the calls that
    come into your business. That includes:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Call recordings and written transcripts</li>
    <li>Caller phone numbers, names and any details a caller gives</li>
    <li>Appointments booked, and the calendar entries created for them</li>
    <li>Text messages sent and received on your behalf</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This information belongs to you, not to us. We access it to set your
    assistant up, to correct it during the tuning period, and to fix faults you
    report. We do not sell it, rent it, share it with advertisers, or use one
    customer's records to do anything for another customer.
  </p>

  <h2>Call recording and consent</h2>
  <p>
    Some jurisdictions, including around a dozen US states, require every party
    on a call to consent to it being recorded rather than just one. Where that
    applies, we configure a spoken notice at the start of the call as part of
    your setup. If your situation is unusual, tell us before you go live and we
    will work out the right arrangement.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else touches your data</h2>
  <p>
    We build on third-party infrastructure rather than running our own
    telephony and speech systems, so your calls pass through the providers we
    use for phone numbers, voice processing, and calendar connections. They act
    on our instructions and are bound by their own agreements. We will tell you
    which providers are involved in your setup if you ask, and you are entitled
    to ask.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Recordings and transcripts are kept for as long as your service is running,
    or for a shorter period if you ask us to set one. Enquiries that do not
    become customers are deleted once the conversation has clearly ended. When
    you leave, you can export everything, and we will delete our copies on
    request.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what we hold about you, ask for a copy of it, ask us to
    correct it, or ask us to delete it. Email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a> and you will get an
    answer inside one business day. There is no fee and no form.
  </p>

  <h2>Cold outreach</h2>
  <p>
    We contact businesses directly, using business contact details, to introduce
    what we do. If you would rather not hear from us, reply and say so, or email
    the address above. You will be removed and not contacted again, and you do
    not have to explain why.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes in a way that affects existing customers, we will
    email them about it rather than quietly editing the page and hoping nobody
    notices.
  </p>
</Legal>
